  "TITLE": "Network Effects:<br>Why Crowds Compound",
  "LEAD": "A phone is worthless to its only owner, yet every new subscriber adds a possible connection to everyone already there &mdash; so users grow linearly while possible links grow roughly with their square. Hemoglobin works the same way: each oxygen that binds makes the next one bind more easily, which is why it loads up sharply instead of gradually.",
